@@ -0,0 +1,157 @@
+# Hegel property-based testing report: `rumqttc` (rumqtt) MQTT codec
+
+Target: the sans-IO MQTT packet codec inside the `rumqttc` crate — MQTT 3.1.1 in
+`rumqttc/src/mqttbytes/` (v4 packets + topic matching) and MQTT 5.0 in
+`rumqttc/src/v5/mqttbytes/v5/`. `hegeltest` 0.28.2 was added as a dev-dependency
+with `--ignore-rust-version` (rumqttc pins `rust-version = 1.64.0`, hegeltest
+needs 1.86 — a maintainer decision if these tests are upstreamed).
+
+## Properties tested
+
+All tests live in the existing source files' test modules, next to the unit
+tests for the same code.
+
+`rumqttc/src/mqttbytes/mod.rs` (remaining-length varint):
+
+1. **`remaining_length_encode_decode_roundtrip`** — for any length 0..=268_435_455
+   (with the 127/128/16383/16384/2097151/2097152 boundaries boosted),
+   `write_remaining_length` produces the byte count given by an independent
+   MQTT-3.1.1 table oracle, continuation bits are set on every byte but the
+   last, and `length()` decodes back both the value and the byte count.
+2. **`remaining_length_above_max_is_rejected`** — lengths > 268_435_455 return
+   `PayloadTooLong` and write nothing.
+3. **`length_decode_never_panics_and_stays_in_range`** — `length()` on arbitrary
+   bytes never panics, only returns `InsufficientBytes`/`MalformedRemainingLength`
+   errors, and any decoded value fits in 4×7 bits.
+
+`rumqttc/src/mqttbytes/v4/mod.rs` (whole-packet codec, all 14 v4 packet types
+via a composite generator covering Connect with last-will/login, Publish with
+QoS/dup/retain/pkid/payloads up to 8 KB, Subscribe/SubAck/Unsubscribe/acks/pings):
+
+4. **`v4_packet_write_read_roundtrip`** — `write` then `read` recovers the exact
+   packet, and only the frame is consumed (drawn trailing bytes stay in the buffer).
+5. **`v4_size_agrees_with_write`** — `Packet::size()` == `write()`'s return value
+   == bytes actually written.
+6. **`v4_read_never_panics_on_arbitrary_bytes`** — `Packet::read` on arbitrary
+   bytes with arbitrary max sizes never panics.
+7. **`v4_truncated_packet_reports_insufficient_bytes`** — every strict prefix of
+   a valid frame yields `InsufficientBytes(n)` with `1 <= n <= missing` (the
+   tokio codec relies on this), and the completed buffer decodes to the original.
+8. **`v4_incoming_max_packet_size_is_honored`** — reading succeeds at
+   `max == remaining_len` and fails with `PayloadSizeLimitExceeded(remaining_len)`
+   for any smaller max (no off-by-one).
+9. **`v4_outgoing_max_packet_size_is_honored`** — writing fails with
+   `OutgoingPacketTooLarge` (leaving the buffer untouched) for any
+   `max < size()`, succeeds at `max == size()`.
+10. **`v4_packet_sequence_roundtrip`** — up to 5 packets encoded back-to-back
+    into one buffer decode back in order (Connect restricted to first position;
+    see Bug 2).
+
+`rumqttc/src/mqttbytes/topic.rs` (topic/filter matching):
+
+11. **`derived_wildcard_filters_are_valid`** — a filter derived from a random
+    topic by substituting `+` levels and/or a `#` tail passes `valid_filter`.
+12. **`topic_matches_filter_derived_from_it`** — `matches(topic, filter)` holds
+    for such derived filters.
+
+`rumqttc/src/v5/mqttbytes/v5/publish.rs` + `v5/mod.rs` (MQTT 5):
+
+13. **`v5_publish_write_read_roundtrip`** — v5 Publish with generated
+    `PublishProperties` (payload format, expiry, topic alias, response topic,
+    correlation data, user properties, subscription identifier, content type)
+    roundtrips exactly through `Packet::write`/`Packet::read`.
+14. **`v5_publish_size_agrees_with_write`** — generalizes the existing
+    `length_calculation` unit test to arbitrary publishes.
+15. **`v5_truncated_publish_reports_insufficient_bytes`** — as property 7, for
+    v5 frames.
+16. **`v5_read_never_panics_on_arbitrary_bytes`** — v5 `Packet::read` robustness.
+
+Plus 5 deterministically pinned KNOWN FAILURE tests (see Suspected bugs).
+
+## Test results
+
+`cargo test -p rumqttc --lib`: **89 passed, 5 failed** — the 5 failures are all
+`known_failure_*` tests that deterministically pin real bugs (below). All other
+properties are green at the default 100 cases and were also run at
+`test_cases = 1000` (10x exploratory pass; that pass is what exposed Bug 5).
+Liveness was verified by temporarily inverting the size assertion in property 5
+(hegel shrank it to the minimal `PubAck { pkid: 0 }`); the change was reverted
+and the `.hegel` failure DB removed. `.hegel/` was added to `.gitignore`.
+
+## Suspected bugs
+
+All five are pinned by failing tests that reproduce on every run.
+
+1. **`matches()` panics on topics starting with a multi-byte UTF-8 character**
+   (`src/mqttbytes/topic.rs:64`, same code duplicated in
+   `src/v5/mqttbytes/mod.rs:98`). `topic[..1]` slices by byte index to test for
+   a leading `'$'`; `matches("é/a", "+")` panics with "byte index 1 is not a
+   char boundary". Should be `starts_with('$')`.
+   Pinned: `known_failure_matches_never_panics_on_multibyte_topics`.
+
+2. **`Connect::write` corrupts non-empty buffers (v4)**
+   (`src/mqttbytes/v4/connect.rs:112`). `flags_index = 1 + count + 2 + 4 + 1`
+   is an absolute buffer index, not relative to the packet start, so a Connect
+   encoded after any other packet (the tokio `Encoder` reuses `dst`) patches
+   its connect-flags byte into the wrong packet's bytes: the will/login flags
+   are lost and a byte of earlier data is overwritten. Writing two Connects
+   into one buffer overwrites the *first* packet's flags with the second's.
+   Pinned: `known_failure_v4_connect_written_after_another_packet_roundtrips`.
+
+3. **Same `flags_index` bug in the v5 `Connect::write`**
+   (`src/v5/mqttbytes/v5/connect.rs:99,127`).
+   Pinned: `known_failure_v5_connect_written_after_another_packet_roundtrips`.
+
+4. **`write_mqtt_bytes` silently truncates the u16 length prefix for fields
+   >= 65536 bytes** (`src/mqttbytes/mod.rs:277`, duplicated at
+   `src/v5/mqttbytes/v5/mod.rs:448`). `stream.put_u16(bytes.len() as u16)`
+   wraps, but the full data is still written, so `Packet::write` reports
+   success while emitting a corrupt frame: a 65536-byte topic decodes as an
+   empty topic with the topic bytes reinterpreted as payload. Should return an
+   error for oversized fields.
+   Pinned: `known_failure_v4_publish_topic_longer_than_u16_roundtrips`.
+
+5. **v5 `PublishProperties::read` double-counts the property-type byte for
+   subscription identifiers** (`src/v5/mqttbytes/v5/publish.rs:229`):
+   `cursor += 1 + id_len` after `cursor += 1` was already applied at the loop
+   top. With 3+ subscription identifiers the cursor overruns the property
+   length, the loop exits early, and the remaining property bytes are silently
+   misparsed as message payload (found by the 10x run, shrunk to
+   `subscription_identifiers: [0, 0, 0]`). `SubscribeProperties::read`
+   (`src/v5/mqttbytes/v5/subscribe.rs:237`) has the identical double-count —
+   marked there with a `TODO: Validate 1 +. Tests are working either way`.
+   Pinned: `known_failure_v5_publish_multiple_subscription_ids_roundtrip`;
+   the sibling v5 publish generators cap subscription identifiers at one, with
+   a comment referencing the pin.
+
+## Unsound properties abandoned
+
+- **Roundtrip of `Login`/`PublishProperties` "empty" values**: `Some(Login)`
+  with both fields empty and `Some(PublishProperties)` with no fields set are
+  written with zero flags/zero property length and correctly read back as
+  `None` — they are not wire-representable, so generators construct only
+  representable values rather than asserting a false equality.
+- **pkid roundtrip at QoS 0**: the pkid field is not on the wire for QoS 0
+  publishes (and `pkid == 0` is rejected for QoS > 0), so generators emit only
+  wire-representable (qos, pkid) combinations instead of asserting that an
+  ignored field survives.
+- **Exact `InsufficientBytes(n)` == missing bytes**: when the fixed header
+  itself is truncated the codec only promises a lower bound (it asks for 1 more
+  byte to finish the varint), so the property asserts `1 <= n <= missing`
+  rather than equality.
+
+## Skill feedback
+
+- The "do one exploratory high-count run" step earned its keep: Bug 5 needs
+  three property-cursor overruns to leave leftover bytes, and never appeared at
+  100 cases across several full runs; it appeared immediately at 1000.
+- The "exclude known-buggy input from sibling properties, with a comment
+  referencing the canonical test" guidance worked well here three times
+  (string lengths capped at 65535, Connect restricted to first position in the
+  sequence property, subscription identifiers capped at one).
+- The MSRV note in the Rust reference (`--ignore-rust-version`) was exactly
+  what was needed for rumqttc's `rust-version = 1.64.0` pin.
+- `pretty_assertions`' colored diff in the shrunk counterexample output made
+  the Bug 5 diagnosis (payload contamination + missing third identifier)
+  readable at a glance — no friction adding hegel tests to modules that
+  explicitly import `pretty_assertions::assert_eq`.
